{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Network Resources in Information Systems"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about network resources in information systems."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts. Design the data structure, starting from the conceptual model determined in the systems analysis, using database IT tools, according to regulation and established standards."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. Recognizes simple ideas on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Future With Will in Negative Form and the Modal Verb Might</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">will </span> in <span class=\"strong\">negative statements</span> to talk about events we feel are not likely to happen. On the other hand, we can use the modal verb <span class=\"strong\">might</span> to talk about actions that are likely to happen. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "To create statements with <span class=\"strong\">will in negative form</span>, you just need to follow this grammatical structure: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Will Not (Won't) </span> + Verb + Complement</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>We <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> need a LAN connection. Our office is very small.</i> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>She <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> use many devices at the same time.</i> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the other hand, if we want to express a certain level of probability of a future event, we can use the modal verb <span class=\"strong\">might. </span> Take a look at the following grammatical structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Might</span> + Verb + Complement</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>We<span class=\"strong\"> might</span> need a faster internet connection.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>He <span class=\"strong\">might</span> be interested in switching to LAN.</i> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can use sentences with<span class=\"strong\"> will not</span> and sentences along with the modal verb <span class=\"strong\">might</span> to create statements. Check the following examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>We <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> need a LAN connection, we<span class=\"strong\"> might</span> invest in a PAN connection instead.</i> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>She <span class=\"strong\">might</span> have connectivity issues. Those modems <span class=\"strong\">won't</span> reach all the offices. </i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We might need to chance our network resources. Now that our company is growing, I won't accept any type of system issue."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It might take us longer than we expect to expand our current network but I'm sure the system won't experience systematic failures."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Our internet speed won't be slow ever again and this might allow us to increase productivity."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Types of Computer Networks</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A computer network is a set of devices connected together to share resources and information. There are different types of networks such as LAN, MAN, WAN, PAN, among others. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can classify networks by their size. These networks include wired and wireless connections. Sometimes, we can find networks that are completely wired or completely wireless; it all depends on the specific necessities of the users. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Personal Area Network (PAN): </span>  This network is the smallest in size and it is very common to find at home or in a small office. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Local Area Network (LAN): </span>  Most companies use this network. It is cheap and secure. Some companies rather have wired connections in order to have a faster network. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Metropolitan Area Network (MAN): </span>  This is the type of network that you can find in distribution centers, small regions or cities. Some universities with big campuses prefer to have a MAN connection in order to cover all the buildings in it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Wide Area Network (WAN): </span>  This is the biggest one in size. It can cover an entire country, continent or even the whole world.  "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "systematic failure "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "collapse or breakdown of a system"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm sure the system won't experience systematic failures."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "by far "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "definitely, undoubtedly, considerably, without a doubt"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I just did a speed test, and the internet is by far faster than ever."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "within budget "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "spending an amount of money that doesn't exceed the amount expected"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We still need to make some changes; don't worry, we are within budget."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "expanse "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large extension of area or territory"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We will switch to MAN which covers an expanse twenty times bigger."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "extranet "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a company's network of computers accessible from the outside with permission of an administrative or IT authority"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I am working on a robust LAN computer network with intranet and extranet services."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for information about network resources in information systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Search for information about any company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify different network resources you would implement in that company and compare them. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down a short paragraph explaining the network resources you will implement in the company and the comparison among those resources. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your paragraph with the class and discuss. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search for information about network resources in information systems. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify and compare different network resources to implement in a company."}, {"type": "text", "content": " write a paragraph explaining the network resources I would implement in a company and compare. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share and discuss information related to network resources. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can describe network resources in information systems."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can compare different resources that take part in info systems."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can summarize information related to network resources in info systems."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What devices do you usually use to connect to the internet? What internet connection do you use with that device?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the benefits of wireless connections?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "What type of network do you need?"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "img_p